        "physical_scope": "The adopted universal range condition for thermal-equilibrium partners in the declared contact family; it is an operational assumption, not an empirical thermometer calibration."
      },
      {
        "id": "post-td-equilibrium-join-coherence",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Equilibrium-join coherence C1",
        "statement": "Adopt **C1 (equilibrium-join coherence)**: whenever $x\\sim_T y$, the joined state $J_{ij}(x,y)$ is thermally equivalent to each constituent, $J_{ij}(x,y)\\sim_T x$ and $J_{ij}(x,y)\\sim_T y$, using the model’s declared nested-join identifications.\n\nC1 is an additional postulate of this completed contact branch. The source’s Theorem 4.8 is stated with T1–T4; the local conditional calibrator route uses the constituent-to-join bridge in addition to the stronger T5 range assumption. Neither fact licenses deriving C1 from $u=u_i+u_j$, from T1–T4, or from transitivity alone. The displayed source supports the contact context, not the claim that its bare printed axioms already contain C1.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-thermal-join",
          "post-td-thermal-join-axioms"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-thermal-join": "formulation-prerequisite",
