              "url": "https://www.dlr.de/de/tt/downloads/dokumente/institut/institutsleitung/Entropie.pdf/@@download/file"
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 9,
        "library": "physics",
        "physical_scope": "An explicit coherence assumption for nested thermal joins of equilibrated pairs; it supplements the energy-summing join rule and is not inferred from that rule."
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-contact-product-comparison",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Conditional contact calibrator and product comparison",
        "statement": "For every declared finite family of simple-system domains closed under the thermal joins of [[def-td-thermal-join]], assume the accessibility axioms A1–A6, the simple-system assumptions A7 and S1–S3, the contact assumptions T1–T4, the universal thermal-equilibrium range T5, and equilibrium-join coherence C1, with the exact formulations in [[post-td-accessibility-a1-a6]], [[post-td-simple-system-geometric-axioms]], [[post-td-thermal-join-axioms]], [[post-td-universal-thermal-range]], and [[post-td-equilibrium-join-coherence]]. Then for any two simple types $i,j$, there are $x_0\\prec\\prec x_1$ in $i$ and $y_0\\prec\\prec y_1$ in $j$ such that\n\n$$ (x_0,y_1)\\sim(x_1,y_0). $$\n\nMoreover, for this fixed pair $i,j$, every finite separated product made only from positive scaled copies of $i$ and $j$ satisfies the comparison hypothesis: any two equal-formal-mass states $A,B$ of that product type satisfy $A\\prec B$ or $B\\prec A$. No comparison conclusion for products involving a third primitive type is contained in this pairwise result. These are conditional model deductions. In particular, the conclusion is not claimed from the printed Theorem 4.8 interface with T1–T4 alone; the local mathematical supplier explicitly requires the additional T5 and C1 branch.",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses",
          "def-td-scaled-products-and-comparison",
          "def-td-thermal-join",
          "post-td-accessibility-a1-a6",
          "post-td-equilibrium-join-coherence",
