      {
        "id": "pthm-td-universal-mixing-entropy",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Conditional weak entropy principle across mixing channels",
        "statement": "Let $\\mathcal G\\ne\\varnothing$ be a finite-factor-closed network of [[def-td-cross-type-reaction-network]]. Assume the contact hypotheses of [[pthm-td-entropy-under-product-comparison]] provide a finite real baseline entropy $\\sigma_\\Gamma$ on each type. Also assume that network satisfies A1–A6, its exact decorated-chain cost $F$ has the no-sinks property defined there, and the Axiom of Choice. Then there is a real offset $B(\\Gamma)$ for each type, additive under finite composition and extensive under every positive scaling, such that the corrected entropy\n\n$$S_\\Gamma(x):=\\sigma_\\Gamma(x)+B(\\Gamma)$$\n\nis nondecreasing across every admitted channel transition: if $(\\Gamma,x)\\mathcal R(\\Gamma',y)$, then $S_\\Gamma(x)\\le S_{\\Gamma'}(y)$. The conclusion is weak monotonicity only. It does not assert a no-gap identity, uniqueness of $B$, strict increase, or a global entropy principle for networks that fail the stated hypotheses.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-td-cross-type-reaction-network",
