    "items": [
      {
        "id": "ex-td-positive-log-contact-witness",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Positive logarithmic contact model as a consistency witness",
        "statement": "Take finitely many tagged simple types $i$, each with positive dimensionless coordinates $u>0,v>0$ (numerical energy and work coordinates relative to fixed units). Choose constants $c_i,r_i>0$, reference values $u_{\\star,i},v_{\\star,i}>0$, and $b_i\\in\\mathbb R$, and define\n\n$$s_i(u,v)=c_i\\log\\frac{u}{u_{\\star,i}}+r_i\\log\\frac{v}{v_{\\star,i}}+b_i.$$\n\nFor a scaled tag $t i$, set its coefficients to $tc_i,tr_i,tb_i$ and its reference coordinates to $t u_{\\star,i},t v_{\\star,i}$, so $s_{ti}(tu,tv)=t\\,s_i(u,v)$. On finite separated compounds define the relation by nondecrease of the sum of the constituent entropies. For a thermal join of $i,j$, define the joined entropy at $(U,v_i,v_j)$ as the maximum of $s_i(u_i,v_i)+s_j(u_j,v_j)$ over $u_i,u_j>0$ with $u_i+u_j=U$, and define contact equilibrium by equality of the pair entropy with this maximum. For nested joins, use the same maximum construction recursively.\n\nThis formal model explicitly declares each equilibrium endpoint domain to be the stated positive numerical orthant, with endpoint coordinate map the identity and accessibility the entropy-sum relation above. Its fixed unit map assigns $U=u(1\\,\\mathrm J)$ and each work coordinate $W_a=v_aw_a$ for a fixed positive unit $w_a$; this bookkeeping supplies no material realization. Each primitive tag has a fixed formal composition, while the joined endpoint space is the positive orthant in summed energy and retained work coordinates with the summed composition. A scaled copy transports these coordinates and that composition and retains its distinct tag, exactly as in the declared join interface. This provides a nondegenerate consistency witness for the order, geometric, contact, T5, and C1 assumptions on this positive-coordinate family. It supplies no measured parameter values or empirical claim.",
        "deps": [
          "cor-mean-value-theorem",
          "def-natural-logarithm",
          "def-real-power",
          "def-td-scaled-products-and-comparison",
          "def-td-thermal-join",
          "post-td-accessibility-a1-a6",
          "post-td-equilibrium-join-coherence",
          "post-td-simple-system-geometric-axioms",
          "post-td-thermal-join-axioms",
          "post-td-universal-thermal-range",
          "thm-exponential-two-point-convexity",
          "thm-natural-logarithm-laws",
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-natural-logarithm": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-real-power": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-td-scaled-products-and-comparison": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-thermal-join": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-accessibility-a1-a6": "physical-assumption",
